/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# Exception: the throwaway key CI signs test builds with.
#
# It is committed on purpose. Without a fixed key, Gradle falls back to a debug
# key that the build machine generates fresh every run, so every APK is signed
# differently and Android refuses to install one over another — it just says
# "App not installed" and does not explain why.
#
# This key is worthless to a thief: it is not the Play upload key, its password
# is in the workflow file, and an APK signed with it cannot be published. Your
# real key lives in key.properties, which stays ignored above.
!test-signing.jks
